SDCC run time helpers for the Fuzix Z80 kernel

The kernel assembly code uses the classic SDCC calling convention where all
arguments are passed on the stack and results come back in L/HL/DEHL.
SDCC 4.2 changed the default to a register based convention (__sdcccall(1))
and the z80.lib it ships is only built for that convention. Linking the
kernel against it, or compiling the kernel with the new default, silently
produces a kernel that crashes.

The kernel is therefore compiled with --sdcccall 0 where the compiler
supports it, and linked against this small library which is compiled with
exactly the same compiler and options as the kernel. The C files are the
generic implementations from the SDCC library sources (GPL with the
linking exception, see the headers). The .s files are small hand written
helpers for the old calling convention.

No routine is pulled from the SDCC z80.lib any more, so any helper missing
here shows up as an undefined symbol at link time rather than as a silent
ABI mismatch.
